  "claim": {
    "informal": "Every finite irreducible nonnegative real matrix has a positive Perron eigenvalue and strictly positive right and transpose-right modes with the same eigenvalue. The corresponding discrete Doob transform is nonnegative and row-stochastic, and the normalized biorthogonal distribution piStar is strictly positive, sums to one, and is stationary.",
    "formal_core": [
      "finite nonempty index type",
      "real square matrix",
      "Matrix.IsIrreducible, which includes entrywise nonnegativity",
      "positive right eigenmode from the external Perron-Frobenius theorem",
      "positive transpose-right mode from Perron-Frobenius applied to the transpose",
      "Perron-root equality under transpose",
      "finite discrete Doob cancellation",
      "positive finite survivor normalization",
      "nonnegative row-stochastic discrete Doob transform",
      "strictly positive normalized stationary distribution"
    ]
  },
